.TH VDJ-UI 1 "September 2026" "vdj-ui 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vdj-ui \- Qt GUI for Virtual DJ (renders ProLink beat grids)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdj-ui
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vdj-ui
is a Qt-based GUI for Virtual DJ that renders real-time beat positions from
Pioneer CDJ/XDJ ProLink networks. It is designed for nightclub use with a dark
theme, keyboard operation, and real-time beat grid rendering for up to five
decks.
.PP
A single-page application provides a deck area (one horizontal row per deck),
a track browser, a now-playing display, and a status bar showing network and
master state. The VDJ and its physical decks are connected over the ProLink
network; the relative beat position of each deck is rendered as a moving
vertical line across a 4/4 beat grid aligned across all deck rows.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \fB\-\-mock-beat\fR
Run with interior/mock beat data so the grid scrolls without a connected
network (used for development and testing).
.TP
.B \fB\-\-mock-vdj\fR
Provide a mock VDJ so deck controls can be exercised without hardware.
.TP
.B \fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable debug mode at startup: show the packet log dock panel and enable
packet logging to the configured log file.
.TP
.B \fB\-\-link\-export\fR \fIFOLDER\fR
Experimental. Open the rekordbox export in \fIFOLDER\fR in the browser and serve it to the other decks like a player with a USB stick in it, once connected
(the Network menu has a checkbox "Export the Loaded Database as a LINK Player" for the database that is open; off by default). See doc/link\-export.md.
.TP
.B \fB\-\-rekordbox\-mode\fR \fIEXPORT\fR
Experimental. Open the Rekordbox PC mode panel and start pretending to be a rekordbox PC that serves the rekordbox export
in the folder \fIEXPORT\fR (the one containing PIONEER/rekordbox/export.pdb) to the decks. The same mode can be started
from the Network menu. Options: \fB\-\-rb\-iface\fR \fINAME\fR, \fB\-\-rb\-name\fR \fINAME\fR (computer name shown on the decks),
\fB\-\-rb\-device\fR \fIN\fR (default 17), \fB\-\-rb\-log\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR,
\fB\-\-rb\-unknown\-policy\fR \fIignore|empty|close\fR, \fB\-\-rb\-nfs\-exports\fR \fIA,B\fR (mount names offered to the decks, default /), \fB\-\-rb\-nfs\-export\-style\fR \fIlist|group|empty|unavailable\fR (how mountd EXPORT is answered), \fB\-\-rb\-no\-serve\fR (do not serve the files over NFS; by default the
export folder is served read-only, portmapper on UDP 50111, mountd 50112, nfs 2049). Do not use together with Network > Connect or ADJ (same UDP ports).
See doc/rekordbox\-mode.md.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F11
Toggle full screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Toggle the debug packet log panel.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.PP
Play/pause, sync to master, become master, copy BPM, and pitch nudge all have
configurable keyboard shortcuts for low-light operation (see
.BR KeyboardShortcuts ).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration and state are stored as flat files under
.B /etc/vdj-ui/
(or the user cache directory) and should be readable and writable by the
normal user (UID 1000). The directory contains joystick mappings and USB/MIDI
routing.
.SH NETWORK
.B vdj-ui
can listen on a selectable network interface for ProLink packets, optionally
participate as a VDJ in sync, NFS read, and NFS publish. The Network > AutoIP
menu item starts the avahi-autoipd based link-local address helper (via a polkit
GUI prompt for root). NFS mounts from connected players are managed
automatically and released on shutdown.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/vdj-ui/
Configuration directory (user 1000 read-write).
.TP
.B ~/.cache/vdj-ui/mnt/
Mount points for player NFS shares.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success (normal quit), non-zero if the application fails to start.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at the project repository. Debug mode with packet logging may
impact performance on low-power targets such as the Raspberry Pi and is
disabled by default.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cpack (1),
.BR mount (8)
